# Autopilot Refactoring Plan — Fix the Drift

## The Problem

Autopilot was designed as a **thin coordinator** that delegates to specialized copilots.
Instead, it absorbed all the logic (~339 lines) while the copilots shrank to passthrough wrappers.

### Drift Summary

| File | Lines Now | Intended Role | Actual Role |
|---|---|---|---|
| [autopilot.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart) | **339** | Thin entry point / coordinator | Does everything |
| [copilot_data.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart) | **25** | Owns all data mutations | Redundant passthrough |
| [copilot_state.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart) | **80** | Owns all UI state + scoping | Redundant passthrough |
| [copilot_route.dart](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart) | **58** | Should own navigation lifecycle | Dumb model class |

---

## The Fix — Three Moves

### Move 1: [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25) owns [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34)

**Move FROM [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339):**
- `DataSet dataSet` field → lives inside [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25)
- [data(key)](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#253-254), [setData()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#255-261), [patchData()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#262-268) → become methods on [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25)

**[CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25) after refactor:**
```dart
class CopilotData {
  CopilotData(this._onChanged);

  final VoidCallback _onChanged;
  final DataSet _dataSet = DataSet();

  dynamic operator [](String key) => _dataSet[key];
  T? get<T>(String key) => _dataSet.get<T>(key);

  void set(String key, dynamic value, {bool notify = true}) {
    _dataSet[key] = value;
    if (notify) _onChanged();
  }

  void patch(Map<String, dynamic> values, {bool notify = true}) {
    _dataSet.patch(values);
    if (notify) _onChanged();
  }

  Map<String, dynamic> snapshot() => _dataSet.snapshot();

  void clear({bool notify = true}) {
    _dataSet.clear();
    if (notify) _onChanged();
  }
}
```

**Access pattern:** `autopilot.data['key']` or `autopilot.data.set('key', value)`

---

### Move 2: [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80) owns [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117) + all scoping logic

**Move FROM [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339):**
- `StateSet stateSet` field → lives inside [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- `_currentPaperScope`, `_currentPaperI`, `_templateScopes` → live in [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [mountPaper()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#113-133), [mountTemplate()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#134-150), [mountCurrentTemplate()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#172-190) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [paperScopeFor()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#191-195), [templateScopeFor()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#196-200) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [setChromeState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#151-161), [patchChromeState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#162-171) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [paperState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#201-203), [setPaperState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#204-215), [patchPaperState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#216-226) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [templateState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#227-229), [setTemplateState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#230-241), [patchTemplateState()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#242-252) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)
- [clearTemplateScope()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#269-276), [clearPaperScope()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#277-299) → methods on [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)

**[CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80) after refactor owns:**
- The [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117) instance
- All 3-tier scoped state (chrome / paper / template)
- Paper and template mount/clear lifecycle
- Scope key generation

**It receives the current route scope from Autopilot** (or from CopilotRoute) to build scope keys.

---

### Move 3: [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) owns navigation lifecycle

**Rename concept:** The current [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) class becomes `RouteSpec` (or `RouteModel`) — it stays as the data model.

**New [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) becomes the navigator copilot:**

**Move FROM [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339):**
- `_currentRoute` field → lives inside [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58)
- [navigate()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#94-97), [mountRoute()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#98-112), [clearRoute()](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#300-327) → methods on [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58)
- Route-related chrome state syncing (`route.path`, `route.scope`, etc.)

**[CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) after refactor:**
```dart
class CopilotRoute {
  CopilotRoute({required this.state, required this.onChanged});

  final CopilotState state;       // to sync route info into chrome state
  final VoidCallback onChanged;

  RouteSpec? _current;
  RouteSpec? get current => _current;

  void navigate(String rawRoute, {bool notify = true}) {
    mount(RouteSpec.parse(rawRoute), notify: notify);
  }

  void mount(RouteSpec route, {bool notify = true}) {
    clear(notify: false);
    _current = route;
    state.patchChrome({
      'route.path': route.path,
      'route.scope': route.scopeKey,
      'route.app': route.appName,
      'route.pageSpecId': route.pageSpecId,
      'route.optionalId': route.optionalId,
    });
    if (notify) onChanged();
  }

  void clear({bool notify = true}) {
    _current = null;
    state.patchChrome({
      'route.path': null,
      'route.scope': null,
      'route.app': null,
      'route.pageSpecId': null,
      'route.optionalId': null,
    });
    if (notify) onChanged();
  }

  String get currentScopeKey => _current?.scopeKey ?? 'default';
}
```

**The current [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) model class** gets renamed to `RouteSpec`:
```dart
class RouteSpec {
  const RouteSpec({required this.appName, required this.pageSpecId, this.optionalId});
  // ... existing parse/toJson/path/scopeKey logic stays identical
}
```

