---

## Execution Order

1. **Rename** current [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58) → `RouteSpec` (file: `route_spec.dart`)
2. **Fatten [CopilotState](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_state.dart#6-80)** — move all state/scoping logic from Autopilot into it
3. **Fatten [CopilotData](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_data.dart#4-25)** — move DataSet ownership from Autopilot into it
4. **Create new [CopilotRoute](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/copilot_route.dart#1-58)** — move navigation lifecycle from Autopilot into it
5. **Slim Autopilot** — remove moved code, hold copilots as `late final` fields
6. **Update call sites** — `autopilot.mountPaper(...)` → `autopilot.state.mountPaper(...)`
7. **Run tests** to confirm nothing broke

---

## Rules Going Forward

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **Autopilot never directly touches [DataSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/data_set.dart#2-34) or [StateSet](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/state_set.dart#1-117)** — always goes through a copilot.
> - **New runtime concerns get a new copilot** — don't add methods to Autopilot.
> - **Copilots receive `VoidCallback onChanged`** — they don't hold an [Autopilot](file:///Users/Shared/dev/git/genrp/lib/core/agent/autopilot.dart#9-339) reference (avoids circular dependency).
